format 1
adapter curriculum 1
unit: radioactivity

objective u2-parent-daughter
statement: Name the nucleus that decays (parent) and the nucleus it becomes (daughter).

item u2-l1-fill-parent
type: fill
surfaces: lesson
surfaces: practice
surfaces: review
references: ref-openstax-chem-21-3

prompt:
    The nucleus that decays is the ___.

mode: bank

bank:
    {"id":"parent","label":"parent"}
    {"id":"daughter","label":"daughter"}
    {"id":"radiation","label":"radiation"}

answer: parent

explanation:
    The nucleus that decays is the parent. The nucleus it becomes is the daughter.

item u2-l1-match-names
type: match
surfaces: lesson
surfaces: practice
surfaces: review
references: ref-openstax-chem-21-3

prompt:
    Match each name to what it means.

pairs:
    {"id":"parent","left":"Parent","right":"The nucleus that decays"}
    {"id":"daughter","left":"Daughter","right":"The nucleus it becomes"}
    {"id":"radiation","left":"Radiation","right":"What comes out when it changes"}

explanation:
    The parent is the nucleus that decays. The daughter is the nucleus it becomes. Radiation is what comes out.

item u2-x-daughter-name
type: choice
surfaces: practice
surfaces: checkpoint
surfaces: review
references: ref-openstax-chem-21-3

prompt:
    A nucleus decays into a new nucleus. What is the new nucleus called?

options:
    {"id":"daughter","label":"The daughter"}
    {"id":"parent","label":"The parent","note":"The parent is the nucleus that decays."}
    {"id":"radiation","label":"The radiation","note":"Radiation is what comes out, not the new nucleus."}

answer: daughter

explanation:
    The new nucleus is the daughter. The one that decayed is the parent.

item u2-x-fill-daughter
